{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Continuous Deployment.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Continuous Deployment.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"continuous deployment continuous deployment","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Continuous Deployment.md","fileName":"Continuous Deployment.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Continuous Deployment","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 15:58\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Live Game Operations]], [[Continuous Integration and Delivery]] [[Cloud Messaging Caching and Operations Patterns]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Live Game Operations","Continuous Integration and Delivery","Cloud Messaging Caching and Operations Patterns","Continuous Delivery","agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Continuous Deployment.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Continuous Deployment.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"continuous deployment continuous deployment","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Continuous Deployment.md","fileName":"Continuous Deployment.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Continuous Deployment","heading":"Continuous Deployment","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Continuous deployment automatically releases every change that passes the delivery pipeline to the live environment. It extends [[Continuous Delivery]] by removing the manual release decision from the normal flow.\n\nBecause games can have platform, player, and experiential constraints, teams may use staged exposure or feature toggles instead. The principle is to make deployment small, repeatable, observable, and reversible.\n\nAn Azure DevOps pipeline can remove routine manual execution by triggering a build, publishing an artifact, and advancing automated deployment stages when their checks pass. Whether production promotion is automatic determines whether this is continuous deployment rather than continuous delivery.\n\nThe design-patterns source describes different promotion triggers for development, user-acceptance testing, and production. Automated build and test gates can move a change toward release, but an explicit human sign-off before production makes that final stage continuous delivery rather than automatic deployment.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Live Game Operations","Continuous Integration and Delivery","Cloud Messaging Caching and Operations Patterns","Continuous Delivery","agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Continuous Deployment.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Continuous Deployment.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"continuous deployment continuous deployment","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Continuous Deployment.md","fileName":"Continuous Deployment.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Continuous Deployment","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf]]\n[[aspnetcore3andreact.pdf]]\n[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Live Game Operations","Continuous Integration and Delivery","Cloud Messaging Caching and Operations Patterns","Continuous Delivery","agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}